---
system: sys-19-billing-subscription
flow_id: invoice-history
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/19-billing-subscription#get-v1billinginvoices
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, BillingService, Stripe, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - GET /v1/billing/invoices?limit=N&offset=M
  - GET /v1/billing/invoices/{invoice_id}/pdf
externals: [Stripe]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - invoice_pdf_unavailable_stripe_unreachable
  - invoice_not_found
  - list_empty
idempotency: GET is naturally idempotent
retry: caller-side exponential backoff on 5xx only
timeout: 3s p99 list; 5s p99 PDF (Stripe-side)
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant BillingService
    participant Stripe
    participant PostgreSQL

    Note over ParentApp: parent in parent_settings → billing history taps "Billing history"

    ParentApp->>Gateway: GET /v1/billing/invoices?limit=N&offset=M and parent JWT Bearer
    Gateway->>BillingService: forward (JWT validated, read-only — 60s freshness not required)
    BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id, date, amount_cents, status, pdf_available, period_start, period_end FROM invoices WHERE household_id={household_id} ORDER BY date DESC LIMIT N OFFSET M
    alt list_empty
        PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: no rows
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {invoices: [], next_offset: null, total: 0}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    else rows_within_30d (read-through local cache)
        PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: invoice rows (within 30d, cached)
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {invoices: [{id, date, amount_cents, status, pdf_available, period_start, period_end}], next_offset, total}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    else rows_older_than_30d (on-demand Stripe fetch)
        PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: invoice rows (older than 30d, pdf_available may be false)
        BillingService->>Stripe: GET /v1/invoices?customer={stripe_customer_id}&created[lte]={cutoff_ts}
        Stripe-->>BillingService: Stripe invoice list
        BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPSERT invoices (backfill cache)
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {invoices: [...], next_offset, total}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    end

    Note over ParentApp: parent taps a row to view PDF

    ParentApp->>Gateway: GET /v1/billing/invoices/{invoice_id}/pdf and parent JWT Bearer
    Gateway->>BillingService: forward
    BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT stripe_invoice_id, pdf_available FROM invoices WHERE id={invoice_id} AND household_id={household_id}
    alt invoice_not_found
        PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: no rows
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 404 invoice_not_found
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 404
    else invoice_pdf_unavailable_stripe_unreachable
        PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: {stripe_invoice_id, pdf_available: true}
        BillingService->>Stripe: GET /v1/invoices/{stripe_invoice_id} (fetch hosted_invoice_url / invoice_pdf)
        Stripe--xBillingService: 5xx / timeout
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 502 invoice_pdf_unavailable_stripe_unreachable
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 502
    else success
        PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: {stripe_invoice_id, pdf_available: true}
        BillingService->>Stripe: GET /v1/invoices/{stripe_invoice_id}
        Stripe-->>BillingService: {invoice_pdf: signed_url (24h expiry)}
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 307 Location: {stripe_signed_pdf_url}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 307 — client follows redirect to Stripe-hosted PDF
    end

    Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: list timeout 3s p99 — PDF timeout 5s p99 (Stripe-side) — GET naturally idempotent — rows older than 30d fetched on-demand from Stripe and cached
